From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "lich.wang" <lich.wang@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:30:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] rpcd: apps_std: optional writable sensor registry

The sensor hub (SSC) of SM8650 writes its registry directory: it opens a
probe file for writing, writes a temporary file and renames it to
parsed_file_list.csv, and stops loading sensors when any of this fails.

When HEXAGONRPCD_WRITABLE_REGISTRY names a host directory, map the whole
persist sensor registry directory (sns_reg_version, parsed_file_list.csv
and registry/) to it and allow the DSP to write there:

- fopen with "w" or "a" creates or truncates regular files directly in
  the registry directory or in its registry/ subdirectory; any other path,
  name with a slash, "." or "..", and symbolic links are refused;
- fwrite (5), fsync (23), fremove (24) and frename (33) are implemented
  for those files only.

Write handles have their own numbers above the hexagonfs descriptors.
Without the variable nothing changes: the registry stays read-only.
